  "notes": "USAGE: {比較|ひかく} is the formal word for comparison. It's commonly used in academic, business, and analytical contexts.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{比較|ひかく}する (to compare)\n・〜と{比較|ひかく}する (to compare with ~)\n・{比較|ひかく}して (by comparison)\n・{比較|ひかく}にならない (incomparable)\n・{比較|ひかく}{的|てき} (relatively, comparatively)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n・{比較|ひかく}{的|てき} (relatively, comparatively)\n・{比較|ひかく}{検討|けんとう} (comparative examination)\n・{比較|ひかく}{文化|ぶんか} (comparative culture)\n・{比較|ひかく}{文学|ぶんがく} (comparative literature)\n・{価格|かかく}{比較|ひかく} (price comparison)\n\nGRAMMAR NOTE: In grammar, {比較|ひかく} is used for comparison expressions:\n・{比較|ひかく}{級|きゅう} (comparative degree)",
